 It also provides other products and services for brakes; mufflers and exhaust systems; and steering, drive train, suspension, and wheel alignment. The company operates its stores under the Monro Auto Service and Tire Centers, Tire Choice Auto Service Centers, Mr. Tire Auto Service Centers, Car-X Tire & Auto, Tire Warehouse Tires for Less, Ken Towery's Tire & Auto Care, Mountain View Tire & Auto Service, and Tire Barn Warehouse brand names. Monro, Inc. was founded in 1957 and is based in Fairport, New York.","ceo_bio":"Mr. Peter D. Fitzsimmons M.D. | CEO, President & Director | Age 68 | Compensation: $2.7M (FY2026)","culture_narrative":"Employs approximately 6K people. Revenue per employee of $180K ranks in the bottom quartile among Consumer Cyclical peers. Each employee generates $6K of free cash flow annually. Stock-based compensation of $602 per employee reflects an ownership culture. CEO compensation is 15\u00d7 revenue per employee (reasonable relative to workforce productivity). Governance score flags moderate compensation governance risk (5/10).","financial_summary":["Monro, Inc. is a small-cap consumer cyclical business with a $328M market cap on $1.2B of annual revenue.","The top line has compounded at -4% over the past three years and +2% annually across the full decade, and a shrinking top line is the hardest headwind any business can overcome.","Returns on capital run at 6% against a 10% cost of capital, which means the business is destroying value with every dollar it reinvests, with gross margins sitting at 38%.","The business throws off $39M in free cash flow \u2014 roughly 3 cents on every revenue dollar, which is the owner-earnings figure that actually belongs to shareholders, and cash conversion sits at 32.42\u00d7 so those profits are backed by real cash.","On the balance sheet, leverage is comfortably conservative at 0.6\u00d7 net debt/EBITDA, and thin 1.2\u00d7 interest coverage leaves no room for a bad year.","Management returns a meaningful 10.6% of market cap to owners through dividends and buybacks, a strong signal of disciplined capital allocation, and insiders hold 5.6% of the shares, and profit capture is only 0.2\u00d7 the fair share, suggesting no structural edge inside its industry."],"sector_headwinds":[{"text":"Altman Z in the distress zone (1.3) \u2014 the kind of balance-sheet risk that can make a loss permanent","sev":"red","cat":"quality"},{"text":"Very elevated short interest (41.4% of float) \u2014 sophisticated money is betting against the business","sev":"red","cat":"sentiment"},{"text":"Payout ratio of 509% leaves essentially no coverage if earnings wobble","sev":"red","cat":"dividend"},{"text":"Low reinvestment-driven growth suggests the compounding engine has stalled","sev":"amber","cat":"growth"},{"text":"Fragmented industry with below-average profit capture \u2014 no moat to protect margins","sev":"amber","cat":"moat"},{"text":"Volatile returns on capital suggest the moat is narrower than a snapshot ROIC implies","sev":"amber","cat":"moat"},{"text":"Revenue growth lags most Consumer Cyclical peers \u2014 losing share inside the profit pool","sev":"amber","cat":"growth"},{"text":"Significant goodwill (47% of assets) from past acquisitions \u2014 a soft asset a conservative appraisal discounts to zero","sev":"amber","cat":"balance_sheet"},{"text":"News tone classified negative across 12 recent articles","sev":"amber","cat":"news"},{"text":"Brand relevance decay \u2014 shifting consumer preferences and social-media-driven trends can strand inventory and invalidate positioning faster than product cycles can adapt.","sev":"amber","cat":"thesis_risk"}],"sector_tailwinds":["Shares offer a 21% margin of safety against estimated fair value","Market is pricing in lower growth than the company has historically delivered","Trading near the bottom of its 52-week range \u2014 the market is offering a discount","Consumer Cyclical sector outperforming the broader market over the past quarter"],"ne